{"units": [{"id": "domos-quote79", "translation": "to let go (I corrected to let down) an anchor in the all-receiving house of strangers."}, {"id": "domos-quote80", "translation": "such things as are fitting for this house."}, {"id": "domos-quote81", "translation": "in the house hope was the healer of the fair Bacchic revel."}, {"id": "domos-quote82", "translation": "and for this house it is utterly bad."}, {"id": "domos-quote83", "translation": "in this house of Atreus."}, {"id": "domos-quote84", "translation": "may old murder no longer breed in the house,"}, {"id": "domos-quote85", "translation": "this would be a burden to carry for the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote86", "translation": "how has it been accomplished for the house?"}, {"id": "domos-quote87", "translation": "what cry do you raise for the house?"}, {"id": "domos-quote88", "translation": "may such a one never dwell with me in the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote89", "translation": "you came as a suppliant, pure and unharmed, to the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote90", "translation": "in the house of Pheres."}, {"id": "domos-quote91", "translation": "for the children and the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote92", "translation": "who has done me many evils in the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote93", "translation": "in wealthy houses."}, {"id": "domos-quote94", "translation": "and she brings a child into the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote95", "translation": "brick-built houses facing the sun."}, {"id": "domos-quote96", "translation": "to the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote97", "translation": "the hearth-houses."}, {"id": "domos-quote98", "translation": "the black-robed Erinys will not come to the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote99", "translation": "leaving, I come to the gold-adorned house."}, {"id": "domos-quote100", "translation": "escort him to the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote101", "translation": "go to the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote102", "translation": "there is some hope that he will come back to the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote103", "translation": "coming to the halls and the hearth-houses."}, {"id": "domos-quote104", "translation": "go now – to the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote105", "translation": "darkness covers the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote106", "translation": "passing by the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote107", "translation": "I did not cast you away to the spear-welcoming house."}, {"id": "domos-quote108", "translation": "having saved my house."}, {"id": "domos-quote109", "translation": "now I am going to the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote110", "translation": "to dwell in well-built houses."}, {"id": "domos-quote111", "translation": "single-rhythmed houses."}, {"id": "domos-quote112", "translation": "I will burn down the house of Amphion."}, {"id": "domos-quote113", "translation": "never yet did a day without hunting send Actaeon empty to the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote114", "translation": "up now, house (thus Hermann for houses)."}, {"id": "domos-quote115", "translation": "when the house of Justice falls."}, {"id": "domos-quote116", "translation": "in pure houses."}, {"id": "domos-quote117", "translation": "they hung up the ancient treasure in the house."}, {"id": "domos-quote118", "translation": "from the house of Loxias."}, {"id": "domos-quote119", "translation": "to the master of this house."}, {"id": "domos-quote120", "translation": "it is not fitting to approach this house."}, {"id": "domos-quote121", "translation": "I ordered them to turn to this house."}, {"id": "domos-quote122", "translation": "for it is not suitable to come to this house."}, {"id": "domos-quote123", "translation": "for this man is a suppliant by custom and a hearth-sharer of my house"}, {"id": "domos-quote124", "translation": "the hearth-sharer of your house."}, {"id": "domos-quote125", "translation": "at the house of Erechtheus."}, {"id": "domos-quote126", "translation": "the house of Artemis."}, {"id": "domos-word1", "translation": "house"}, {"id": "domos-word2", "translation": "houses"}, {"id": "domos-word3", "translation": "from the paternal house"}, {"id": "domos-word4", "translation": "house"}, {"id": "domos-word5", "translation": "course"}, {"id": "domos-word6", "translation": "houses"}, {"id": "domos-word7", "translation": "halls"}, {"id": "domos-word8", "translation": "A. I"}, {"id": "domos-word9", "translation": "he subdued"}, {"id": "domos-word10", "translation": "in the house"}, {"id": "domos-word11", "translation": "in the houses"}, {"id": "domos-word12", "translation": "in the house"}, {"id": "domos-word13", "translation": "in the houses"}, {"id": "domos-word14", "translation": "in the house"}, {"id": "domos-word15", "translation": "house"}, {"id": "domos-word16", "translation": "houses"}, {"id": "domosphales-orth1", "translation": "house-shaking"}, {"id": "domosphales-def1", "translation": "house-shaking"}, {"id": "domosphales-quote1", "translation": "I fear the house-shaking crash of the rain."}, {"id": "donax-orth1", "translation": "reed"}, {"id": "donax-def1", "translation": "reed"}, {"id": "donax-quote1", "translation": "the wax-fastened reed pipe sounds."}, {"id": "donax-quote2", "translation": "and the marsh reed of Bolbe."}, {"id": "doneo-orth1", "translation": "to shake"}, {"id": "doneo-def1", "translation": "to shake"}, {"id": "doneo-quote1", "translation": "shaking and turning the turmoil up and down."}, {"id": "doxa-orth1", "translation": "opinion, judgment"}, {"id": "doxa-def1", "translation": "opinion, judgment"}, {"id": "doxa-def2", "translation": "reputation, glory"}, {"id": "doxa-note1", "translation": "where, because of the strophic verse, δοκαί [opinions] is more probable, which Hermann restored."}, {"id": "doxa-note2", "translation": "about Orestes being out of his mind"}, {"id": "doxa-quote1", "translation": "with the enduring opinion of the soul."}, {"id": "doxa-quote2", "translation": "I would not take the opinion of a slumbering mind."}, {"id": "doxa-quote3", "translation": "opinions are present bringing vain favor."}, {"id": "doxa-quote4", "translation": "whether the opinion of friends will prevail to bring him back."}, {"id": "doxa-quote5", "translation": "what opinions whirl you about?"}, {"id": "doxa-quote6", "translation": "there are no opinions of these sufferings for me."}, {"id": "doxa-quote7", "translation": "and the opinions of men, even very august under the sky."}, {"id": "doxa-word1", "translation": "opinions"}, {"id": "doxazo-orth1", "translation": "to think, suppose"}, {"id": "doxazo-def1", "translation": "to think, suppose"}, {"id": "doxazo-quote1", "translation": "and we think that they have the same things."}, {"id": "doxazo-quote2", "translation": "this is a good omen for everyone to think."}, {"id": "doxazo-quote3", "translation": "how shall I think these things true and seeing?"}, {"id": "doxazo-quote4", "translation": "one will think, hearing the voice of the wretched wife of Tereus' cunning."}, {"id": "dora-orth1", "translation": "skin, hide"}, {"id": "dora-def1", "translation": "skin, hide. See under σίσυρνα."}, {"id": "dora-word1", "translation": "a garment of skins"}, {"id": "dorigambros-orth1", "translation": "sought in marriage by arms"}, {"id": "dorigambros-def1", "translation": "sought in marriage by arms"}, {"id": "dorigambros-quote1", "translation": "the spear-bride and much-contested Helen."}, {"id": "dorikanes-orth1", "translation": "killed by the spear"}, {"id": "dorikanes-def1", "translation": "killed by the spear"}]}